			"notes": "# Better With Discord 1.0.1\n\nPorted to BTA 8.0.1, with pictures of items and inventories, images from Discord in game and many relay fixes.\n\n## Features\n- `[item]` and `[inv]` in chat send a picture of the held item or the whole inventory to Discord, drawn with the game's own textures, font and tooltips.\n- Inventory pictures show your skin and armor, Aether accessories, the Better With Hands offhand slot and Better With Bags backpacks.\n- Backpack contents and maps are drawn inside their tooltip.\n- Images posted on Discord can be held in game as a map with `/preview`. GIFs play.\n- `/playerlist` on Discord answers with a picture of who is online, like the tab list.\n- Markdown works both ways, so bold, italics, underline, strikethrough and spoilers show up on both sides.\n- `@name` in game mentions that person on Discord. `@everyone` and `@here` never ping.\n- Replies, attachments and stickers from Discord show up in the game.\n- The bot status shows how many players are online.\n- A warning is posted when the server stops responding.\n- The console channel can be limited to a list of allowed commands, and every command run from Discord is logged.\n\n## Fixes\n- Discord messages are handled on the server thread.\n- Server nicknames are shown for Discord users.\n- Death messages are translated instead of showing their keys.\n- Joins and leaves are announced through the player list, so kicks are announced too.\n- A deleted webhook is created again automatically.\n- The server start message is sent once the server has started, and the bot shuts down with the server.\n- Console messages lose their colour codes and send stack traces.\n\n## Updating\n- Settings moved to `config/better_with_discord.cfg`. The old JSON config is moved over automatically.\n- `/playerlist` needs the `applications.commands` scope, and pictures need the Embed Links and Attach Files permissions.\n\n## Requirements\n- Minecraft: **BTA 8.0.1**\n- HalpLibe: **6.2.0+8.0.1**\n- Fabric Loader: **0.18.4-bta.11**\n- Java 17\n\n## License\n- The mod now uses a custom license. See LICENSE."
		},
